1
00:00:05,310 --> 00:00:08,100
OK.

2
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,570
If you want to adopt an animal,

3
00:00:10,570 --> 00:00:12,880
first we need to know some references.

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,670
References?

5
00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:16,420
People we know?

6
00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:19,120
Friends, teachers....

7
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:21,490
We need to talk to some people about you.

8
00:00:21,490 --> 00:00:23,760
We want to be sure that you're responsible

9
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,510
and that you can take good care of an animal.

10
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:28,390
Then you have to fill out this form

11
00:00:28,390 --> 00:00:30,950
about your family background.

12
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:32,170
Is that it?

13
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:34,280
No, there's more.

14
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:37,900
We need to know about your history with animals.

15
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,460
Have you ever owned an animal?

16
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:41,020
Yes.

17
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:43,420
We had a cat when I was eight years old.

18
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:44,980
I love cats.

19
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:47,040
Do you have any animals now?

20
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:49,330
Unfortunately, no.

21
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:50,800
Anything else?

22
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,450
We also like to know

23
00:00:52,450 --> 00:00:54,230
your reasons for wanting an animal.

24
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:56,750
Just to hold it and cuddle with it.

25
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,240
Just to have as a pet.

26
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:01,430
I love animals.

27
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:04,640
To have a friend -- a pal.

28
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:08,330
You know, man's best friend is his dog.

29
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:09,550
And one thing more.

30
00:01:09,550 --> 00:01:11,360
If you're under twenty-one years of age ...

31
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:12,300
That's me.

32
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,000
Then an adult must sign for you.

33
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,620
Uh-oh.

34
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:16,880
No problem.

35
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:19,250
My parents will think it's a good idea.

36
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,480
I'll be back with them.

37
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:23,930
If the real owners don't come to claim Gemma ...

38
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:25,470
After forty-eight hours.

39
00:01:25,470 --> 00:01:27,910
But please call first.

40
00:01:27,910 --> 00:01:31,350
Thanks for your information and for being so helpful.

41
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:32,610
It's my pleasure.

42
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:34,220
Nice talking to both of you.

43
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:34,990
Thanks again.

44
00:01:34,990 --> 00:01:37,830
Bye.

45
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:40,590
Maybe the real owners will come to claim her.

46
00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:42,400
Her eyes look so sad.

47
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,970
She must really miss them.

48
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:45,910
I see you're both animal lovers.

49
00:01:45,910 --> 00:01:47,110
We are.

50
00:01:47,110 --> 00:01:48,320
Good-bye, Miss Aborn.

51
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:49,740
We'll call in a couple of days.

52
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:52,990
Good-bye, and thanks for bringing Gemma in.

53
00:01:52,990 --> 00:02:03,630
Bye.

54
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:06,620
I keep thinking about the dog -- about Gemma,

55
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:08,470
alone in the animal shelter.

56
00:02:08,470 --> 00:02:10,480
I know.

57
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:11,970
But I promise you, Alexandra,

58
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:13,720
the dog is just fine.

59
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,970
They're very kind to the animals.

60
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:16,740
I know they are.

61
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:19,600
I mean about her being alone.

62
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,110
Even if they are kind to Gemma,

63
00:02:21,110 --> 00:02:23,990
she's still alone, without her family.

64
00:02:23,990 --> 00:02:25,460
Ready, folks?

65
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:26,770
Are you ready, Alexandra?

66
00:02:26,770 --> 00:02:28,410
Yes, I'm ready.

67
00:02:28,410 --> 00:02:31,320
I'll have the chef's salad, please.

68
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:34,630
I will have a cheeseburger, medium rare,

69
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:37,800
with raw onion, and french fries, please.

70
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:38,930
Anything to drink?

71
00:02:38,930 --> 00:02:41,210
A diet cola, please.

72
00:02:41,210 --> 00:02:43,560
Ginger ale with lots of ice for me, thank you.

73
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:44,330
I've got it.

74
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:46,780
Thanks.

75
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:47,950
Aren't you surprised

76
00:02:47,950 --> 00:02:49,730
that the animal shelter is so careful

77
00:02:49,730 --> 00:02:51,620
about finding homes for the animals?

78
00:02:51,620 --> 00:02:53,650
No, I'm not.

79
00:02:53,650 --> 00:02:55,480
And a cheeseburger, medium rare,

80
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:57,520
with onion and french fries.

81
00:02:57,520 --> 00:03:00,760
And a ginger ale with lots of ice.

82
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:03,530
Salad dressing?

83
00:03:03,530 --> 00:03:05,750
Hey, I wanted you to hear my new sound system

84
00:03:05,750 --> 00:03:08,300
when the dog scratched on the front door.

85
00:03:08,300 --> 00:03:09,270
Let's finish eating,

86
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:11,800
and then we'll go back to my house.

87
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,500
I want you to hear my new tapes.

88
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:35,440
I've got some great new dance music.

89
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,000
Hello.

90
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,420
Stewart residence.

91
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:37,860
Hello.

92
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:39,320
Is Robbie Stewart there?

93
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:39,930
This is he.

94
00:03:39,930 --> 00:03:40,950
Who's this?

95
00:03:40,950 --> 00:03:43,910
This is Linda Aborn from the animal shelter.

96
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:46,680
It's Linda from the animal shelter.

97
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:47,680
Yes, Linda.

98
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:48,810
Hi.

99
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:50,940
We have good news and bad news, Robbie.

100
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:51,970
Oh?

101
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:54,280
The good news is that the Levinsons have come by

102
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,580
to pick up the dog.

103
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:59,430
The bad news is, you won't be able to adopt the dog.

104
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:00,980
That's OK.

105
00:04:00,980 --> 00:04:03,900
Come by one day and look at some of the other dogs.

106
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:05,790
I'm sure there's one for you.

107
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:06,740
Thanks, Robbie.

108
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:10,300
And the Levinsons thank you for bringing their dog to us.

109
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:11,720
Thanks, Linda.

110
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:21,130
Bye.

111
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:22,950
The owners claimed Gemma?

112
00:04:22,950 --> 00:04:24,550
That's right.

113
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:26,820
I'm glad for the dog.

114
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:29,110
I guess I am, too.

115
00:04:29,110 --> 00:04:30,280
She said if I come by,

116
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:34,980
she'll help me find another dog.

117
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:37,980
Come on. Let's dance.
